{"name":"Patina Grey","hex":"#b6c0bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"patina","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paten (a flat type of dish).","The colour or incrustation which age and wear give to (chiefly metallic) objects; especially, the green rust which covers works of art such as ancient bronzes, coins and medals."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green colour, tinted with grey, like that of bronze patina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patina"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Patina","blocks":[{"text":"Patina is a thin layer that variously forms on the surface of copper, brass, bronze, and similar metals and alloys, or certain stones and wooden furniture, or any similar acquired change of a surface through age and exposure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Minneapolis_City_Hall.jpg/330px-Minneapolis_City_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patina","wikidata":"Q428352"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/FraunkircheSouth.jpg/500px-FraunkircheSouth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/FraunkircheSouth.jpg/1280px-FraunkircheSouth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/FraunkircheSouth.jpg/500px-FraunkircheSouth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Dresden Frauenkirche. The church was destroyed during the bombing of Dresden in 1945 and rebuilt from 1993 to 2005 with new material; the stones with the black patina are the parts that survived the firebombing from the original 18th-century church.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFraunkircheSouth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ancienne_unit%C3%A9_de_monnaie_en_cuivre.jpg/500px-Ancienne_unit%C3%A9_de_monnaie_en_cuivre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ancienne_unit%C3%A9_de_monnaie_en_cuivre.jpg/1280px-Ancienne_unit%C3%A9_de_monnaie_en_cuivre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ancienne_unit%C3%A9_de_monnaie_en_cuivre.jpg/500px-Ancienne_unit%C3%A9_de_monnaie_en_cuivre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pre-colonial copper coin formerly used in the Copper Belt (Democratic Republic of the Congo and Zambia). The external layer has been weathered by moisture and rain, leading to the oxidation of copper.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAncienne_unit%C3%A9_de_monnaie_en_cuivre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Chickenvane.jpg/500px-Chickenvane.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip